                <h2>Filter Rows</h2>
                <p>Now narrow the result set using conditions.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <details class="sql-syntax-ref">
            <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> Reference pattern — WHERE, AND, OR</summary>
            <div class="sql-syntax-body">
                <pre><code>-- Match one value exactly
SELECT *
FROM table_name
WHERE status_column = 'Open';

-- AND means both conditions must be true
SELECT *
FROM table_name
WHERE group_column = 'A'
  AND score_column >= 80;

-- OR means either condition can be true
SELECT *
FROM table_name
WHERE type_column = 'Science'
   OR type_column = 'Technology';</code></pre>
                <p><code>WHERE</code> filters rows. <code>AND</code> makes the query stricter; <code>OR</code> widens it to allow either condition.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

