            <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-unlock"></i> Model Answers — School Library</h2>

            <h3>Section 1</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">1</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Keys and structure</strong>
                    <code>STUDENT(StudentID)</code>, <code>BOOK(BookID)</code>, and <code>LOAN(LoanID)</code>.
                    <code>LOAN.StudentID</code> and <code>LOAN.BookID</code> are foreign keys.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">2</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Schema levels</strong>
                    ERD = conceptual schema. Field names, data types, and keys = logical schema. Storage and indexing = physical schema.
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Section 2</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">3</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Example retrieval</strong>
                    <pre><code>SELECT *
FROM STUDENT;

SELECT Title, Author
FROM BOOK;</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Section 3</h3>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">4</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Filtering examples</strong>
                    <pre><code>SELECT FirstName, LastName, TutorGroup
FROM STUDENT
WHERE TutorGroup = '12B';

SELECT Title, Genre
FROM BOOK
WHERE Genre = 'Science' OR Genre = 'Technology';

SELECT *
FROM LOAN
WHERE StudentID = 1003
  AND ReturnStatus = 'On Loan';</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sql-answer-item">
                <span class="sql-answer-num">5</span>
                <div class="sql-answer-body">
                    <strong>Referential integrity</strong>
                    The foreign key in <code>LOAN</code> must match an existing primary key in <code>STUDENT</code>. If student <code>9999</code> does not exist, the row would create an orphan record and should be rejected.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

